# Category test62 History

See `CONTRIBUTING.rst` for details of **required** info/format for each entry,
which **must** added in reverse chronological order (newest at the top). It must **not**
be used as a substitute for writing good git commit messages!


## 2021-12-10 Ben Morgan (test62-V11-00-00)
- Change to new Markdown History format

---

# History entries prior to 11.0

4 August 2021 Ben Morgan (test62-V10-07-01)
- Modernize CMake script allowing test to be built in system testing
  or as a standalone project

18 February 2021, Ben Morgan (test62-V10-07-00)
- Support same CMake version range as core Geant4

11 October 2012, Gabriele Cosmo   (test62-V09-05-01)
- Explicit inclusion of units and constants headers.

05 July 2012, Alberto Ribon   (test62-V09-05-00)
- Update test62.cc to replace the obsolete physics list QGSP_INCL_ABLA
  with QGSP_INCLXX.

15 June 2011, Gunter Folger   (test62-V09-04-01)
- Update test62.in to replace obsolete /run/particle/SetCut by /run/SetCut

9th June 2010 Pekka Kaitaniemi (test62-V09-04-00)
- Switch from built-in physics list to QGSP_INCL_ABLA:
  o Test now covers both model and physics list
  o Reduces useless physics list code bloat
- Added test cases for light ion projectiles
- This tag requires phys-lists-V09-04-27 or later

18th March 2010  Pekka Kaitaniemi (test62-V09-03-00)
- Migration to the new G4[e|Mu|h]MultipleScattering system

7th November 2008  Pekka Kaitaniemi (test62-V09-01-00)
- Use test24 as the basis of a new INCL/ABLA cascade/evaporation system test
- Modifications:
  o Use G4InclAblaCascadeInterface (INCL/ABLA for proton, neutron, pi+, pi-,
  pi0 projectiles)
  o Add Carbon, Lead and Thorium target material definitions
  o Hydrogen target not used in the run macro (H target not supported by INCL)
  o Set the test run energy to 1 GeV (INCL4.2 supports energies 200 MeV - 3
  GeV)

6th December 2005  Gabriele Cosmo
- Trivial changes for support of CLHEP-2.0.X series.

16th March 2004  Gabriele Cosmo
- Fixed compilation warnings.
- Replaced usage of NULL with 0.

4th November 2002  Hans-Peter Wellisch
- created the test
